{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"loved-nerdy-ammonite","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nacli_graph.py hand-rolls the SAME nextPageToken cursor loop three times (its docstrings record that startAt is HTTP-400-rejected on /rest/api/3/search/jql — this is a genuinely different protocol from offset paging). None of the three loops carries a runaway-cursor guard: a server that repeats the same nextPageToken spins the loop forever (the cabc bug class, currently a strict-xfail). The offset pager fetcher._iter_pages already has same-page/stall guards — the cursor loops deserve the same hardening, centralized. Split out of e931-7f1f-8b0c-465b by plan review (bundling + protocol conflation).\n\n## Approach\nOne NEW shared cursor iterator (module-level helper in acli_graph.py or a small _paging.py sibling): drives the POST body's nextPageToken, terminates on isLast:true or null/absent token, and raises a loud RunawayPaginationError when the server returns the same non-null token twice consecutively (fixes the cabc failure mode at the shared seam). All three acli_graph maps consume it; call sites never hand-loop. The iterator parallels fetcher._iter_pages in SHAPE only (it is new code for a different protocol — offset vs cursor; no shared code path). OFFSET-protocol consolidation is explicitly OUT of scope: jira_datacenter/transport.py::_paged_search duplicates _iter_pages but is stable, independently tested, and pinned by bug 9263's structural anti-regression gate; consolidating it is optional debt with its own regression risk and no observed bug class. Held-out structural tests updated in lockstep: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py (pins the three Cloud loops' structure — updated to pin the shared-iterator wiring instead); test_fetcher_pagination_heldout.py and test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py must stay green untouched.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py (three loops -> shared cursor iterator + runaway guard)\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py (re-pin to iterator wiring)\n- OUT of scope: fetcher._iter_pages, jira_datacenter/transport.py::_paged_search and its 9263 gate (offset protocol stays as-is), cc77 transport work (landed).\n\n## Testing\nPer the shared iterator: multi-page traversal, terminal-page via isLast, terminal-page via absent token, same-token-twice -> RunawayPaginationError (kills the cabc class), single-page short-circuit. Wiring: each of the three maps proven to route through the iterator (no residual hand loops — structural assertion). Existing acli_graph behavior suites + fetcher/DC pagination held-outs stay green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] acli_graph.py contains zero hand-rolled pagination loops; all three maps route through the shared cursor iterator (structural test).\n- [ ] Runaway guard: same non-null token twice raises a named error with a test; cabc strict-xfail flipped to a passing guard test or superseded with citation.\n- [ ] Offset pagers untouched and their held-out/structural suites green (fetcher, DC transport, 9263 gate).\n- [ ] discovered_from link to e931-7f1f-8b0c-465b recorded; parent = epic 2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97.","id":"ab7f-f0cc-7384-43a7","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Reconciler: shared cursor-pagination iterator + runaway-token guard in acli_graph"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785771912564803001,"uuid":"db32b2a1-ff81-4bb0-8309-9f8d080a3672"}